    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen running Neovim, a warning about not receiving a DSR response is printed, and a mysterious sequence - `+q4D73` - appears at the top of the screen.\n\n<img width=\"1105\" height=\"640\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a1633947-4f43-41f7-9158-4ecec5319504\" />\n\nThe characters are not actually in the buffer, and going into insert mode and typing something will overwrite them.\n\nI've experienced this on version 0.12.2 (packaged by MSYS2), but also tested the latest nightly and the behaviour remains. It happens both in MinTTY (the default terminal packaged with MSYS2) and in the native Windows command prompt. In Windows 11, however, both version 0.12.2 and the latest nightly work as expected.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```\nnvim --clean\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThere is no warning, and the screen doesn't show any unwanted characters.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.12.2\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, 9.2.452\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nWindows 10 22H2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nMinTTY 3.8.2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm\n\n### Installation\n\nvia pacman, from the MSYS2 package repository",
